WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.300
A Sikh hymn compares the body to a field.

2
00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:06.580
Whatever you sow in this
life, you will harvest.

3
00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:10.750
Sikhs call this karma: actions,
and the results they bring,

4
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.090
in this life or a future one.

5
00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:16.640
At death, Sikhs believe,
the soul is reborn,

6
00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:20.420
again and again, in a
cycle called samsara.

7
00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:25.610
If every action has a result, can
anyone ever escape being born again?

8
00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:30.490
In this mission, you'll find out what
Sikhs believe keeps people in the cycle.

9
00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:33.310
Then you'll learn what
Sikhs mean by liberation,

10
00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:35.600
and why it has two sides.

11
00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:40.360
Your mission: find out whether Sikhs
believe the cycle can end, and how.
